    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39631" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pūrĭfĭcātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		purifico, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a purifying</i>, <i>purification</i>
			(post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">laurus purificationibus adhibetur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					15, 30, 40, § 138</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">religionis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. 8 praef.</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sanguis purificationis suae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Lev. 12, 4</span></i>
			: purificatio, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καθαρμός</span>,
			Gloss. Cyril.</div>
